__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
# The venv lives at .venv.nosync with .venv symlinked to it: this repo sits
# under an iCloud-synced ~/Documents, and iCloud skips paths ending .nosync.
# Syncing a venv corrupts it (duplicated "lib 2/" directories, hidden .pth
# files that CPython then ignores, stale console scripts) and `uv sync`
# reports "Audited N packages" while repairing none of it. Recovery is in
# MAINTAINING.packages.md §2 under Portability.
.venv
.venv.nosync/
# `uv build` output. The maintaining docs tell operators to build wheels
# (wheel-contents and isolated-install checks), so this would otherwise show
# up in `git status` after every documented verification run.
dist/
# Real credential files at any depth (.env, .env.test, .env.provisioning,
# instances/*/.env, ...); the tracked templates are re-included below.
.env*
!.env.example
!*.env.example
!.env.test.example
!.env.provisioning.example
# Skills and agents are owned by the dedicated skills repo, not versioned here;
# the working copy under .claude/ stays on disk but out of this repo's history.
.claude/
.DS_Store
# Corpus data and run logs live under each instance; the explicit patterns
# (rather than bare logs/ and data/ matching at any depth) make the intent
# visible and keep unrelated directories trackable.
instances/*/data/
instances/*/logs/
# Fallback log location for engine-only runs is outside the repo (see
# ingpipe_lib.paths.fallback_log_root), so no repo-root pattern is needed.
